systemctl/svchost service manager; pure-Go sshd/wssh; build.ps1 default dev

- systemctl: systemd-style unit manager on Windows (pure Go). Parses
  *.service INI units (quote-aware ExecStart), four backends - built-in
  svchost service host (wrapped), native service, scheduled task
  (schtasks), masked - with start/stop/restart/enable/disable/status/
  is-active/is-enabled/cat/list-units/list-unit-files/journalctl/
  mask/unmask/daemon-reload. State in %ProgramData%\systemctl.
- svchost: built-in Windows service host (x/sys/windows/svc) replacing
  the external wrapper; hosts ExecStart, taskkill /t process trees,
  GBK/OEM->UTF8 log decoding into <unit>.wrapper.log.
- sshd: pure-Go SSH server (x/crypto/ssh, no OpenSSH install needed) on
  :1022 by default. --auth local validates Windows local users via
  LogonUserW; exec runs `winux sh -c`, shell attaches a ConPTY pseudo
  console running winux sh. sshd --install registers the winux-sshd
  service (manageable via systemctl). Host key auto-generated.
- wssh: pure-Go SSH client (no OpenSSH needed), default port 1022,
  password auth, interactive pty sessions with window-change resize.
- sh -i: force the interactive REPL without a console (used by ConPTY).
- build.ps1: default build is now a dev build stamped with the git
  commit id; -Version x.y.z stamps a formal release.
- ConPTY implemented with direct kernel32 syscalls (CreatePipe/
  CreatePseudoConsole/attribute list/CreateProcess); pty-req and
  window-change parsed per RFC 4254.
- Tests: core ConPTY roundtrip, end-to-end sshd+wssh against a real
  winux.exe process, systemctl read-only paths; smoke 218->224.
- Deps: add golang.org/x/crypto v0.50.0 and golang.org/x/sys v0.40.0
  (pinned, Go 1.25 compatible).